ntial tests for cmd/cat (rel01.1-uc001-cat)\".","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15888,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15888},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4ad9d3f-b159-4e27-8e32-624170b307da","uuid":"4cd6be77-2673-4595-be0e-6ff71d171d4e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01H38bUZyYVAJZKXoosXjdzk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 1 & 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal, implementer-accessible specifications. Man pages omit edge cases, flag interactions, and exit-code contracts.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline per utility — extract (C source) → specify (human-authored PRD + use case) → synthesize (mage-claude-orchestrator drives Claude agent) → verify (differential testing harness). Major components: `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (formatting), `magefiles/` (mage targets).\n\n**Current state**: All generated code lives at `generation-merged` tags (not on the working branch). Specs are complete for cat, wc, sponge, ls, du. No generated code is present on the current branch.\n\n**Current release scope**: Release `01.1` — `rel01.1-uc001-cat`. specstatus: spec_complete, codestatus: not started, testfiles: 0.\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease `01.1` has one use case (`rel01.1-uc001-cat`). Issue #296 already tracks the implementation (\"Implement cmd/cat concatenation and flag processing\"). Per the planning constitution, implementation and tests must be split into separate tasks. No test task exists in the issue tracker for cat. The test task depends on the implementation from #296, but since #296 is an external pre-existing issue (not in this batch), `dependency` is `-1`.\n\n## Step 4 & 5: Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Write differential tests for cmd/cat (rel01.1-uc001-cat)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (glob this directory to find the cat PRD, filename matches prd[NNN]-cat.yaml; read it fully before writing any test)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc001-cat.yaml (actor, trigger, and execution flow for the cat use case)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/ (glob this directory to find the rel01.1 test suite; read it for expected input/output pairs)\n      - pkg/testutils/ (read all files in this package to understand the DiffTest struct and harness API)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (cat implementation being tested; must be present before this test file can compile)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/cat_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: differential tests comparing the Go cat binary against the GNU cat reference binary using pkg/testutils\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement differential tests for basic file concatenation -- reading one or more named files and writing their concatenated contents to stdout -- per the cat PRD file I/O requirements\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement differential tests for all cat flags defined in the PRD (-n, -b, -s, -v, -A, -T, -e, -u), including flag combinations where the PRD specifies combined behavior\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement differential tests for stdin input -- the case where no file arguments are given and the case where \"-\" is passed as an explicit stdin argument -- per the cat PRD stdin requirements\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement differential tests for error conditions (nonexistent file, unreadable file) verifying that both exit code and stderr content match the GNU reference binary exactly\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Use the pkg/testutils DiffTest harness for all test cases; do not write manual golden-file comparisons or inline byte assertions\n      - id: D2\n        text: Set LC_ALL=C in every test case environment map to satisfy the project-wide locale constraint documented in ARCHITECTURE.yaml design decision 6\n      - id: D3\n        text: The GNU reference binary is the Homebrew gcat (or cat from coreutils); locate it following the convention used by other cmd/ test files in this repository -- read at least one existing cmd/*/test file before writing cat_test.go\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/cat/... passes with all differential test cases green against the GNU reference binary\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: Each acceptance criterion in the cat PRD has at least one corresponding named test case in cat_test.go\n      - id: AC3\n        text: Every flag listed in the cat PRD is exercised by at least one test case\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Error condition tests assert both exit code and stderr content match the GNU reference binary output\n      - id: AC5\n        text: cat_test.go compiles cleanly with no warnings under golangci-lint\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15888,"cache_read_input_tokens":19189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15888},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c4ad9d3f-b159-4e27-8e32-624170b307da","uuid":"8112de06-96dc-4c48-8d84-166b21d45069"}
